# CLAUDE.md

This file provides guidance to Claude Code (claude.ai/code) when working with code in this repository.

## Repository Overview

This is the `~/.claude` configuration directory for Claude Code, containing user settings, specialized agents, plugins, conversation history, and project-specific state. This directory controls how Claude Code operates across all projects.

## Key Scripts

```bash
# Initialize slash commands in a new project
~/.claude/init-project-commands.sh

# Switch model provider (anthropic, glm, kimi)
~/.claude/switch-model-provider.sh <provider>

# Interactive Kimi K2 launcher
~/.claude/start-kimi.sh

# Load MCP server secrets before starting Claude
source ~/.claude/.env.claude && claude
```

## Model Aliases (.clauderc)

```
~glm, ~haiku, ~sonnet, ~opus  → GLM models
~kimi, ~kimi-turbo            → kimi-k2-turbo-preview
~kimi-think                   → kimi-k2-thinking-turbo (recommended)
~kimi-think-slow              → kimi-k2-thinking
```

## MCP Servers (settings.json)

Currently configured: filesystem, context7, vercel, playwright, telnyx_api, n8n-mcp, vapi, google-sheets, langsmith

## Global Skills (Available Everywhere)

Skills in `~/.claude/skills/` are globally available without project initialization:

**Research & Analysis (Opus 4.5 Agents)**
- `deep-research` - 6 parallel agents for codebase best practices analysis
- `production-audit` - Production readiness audit (security, performance, reliability)
- `stack-researcher` - Web + Context7 docs research for tech stacks

**Debugging & Fixing**
- `deep-debug`, `smart-fix`, `universal-debugger`, `debugger`

**Development Workflows**
- `tdd-workflow` - Test-driven development
- `git-flow` - Automated git workflows
- `frontend-design` - Distinctive frontend interfaces (updated 2025)
- `mcp-builder` - Build MCP servers
- `skill-creator` - Create new skills

**Frontend (Practical)**
- `frontend` - Build components with animations (auto-detects your stack)
- `responsive` - Deep responsive analysis and fixes for all screens
- `frontend-debug` - Fix visual bugs, layout breaks, z-index wars, CSS conflicts

**Frontend (Reference)**
- `animation-toolkit-2025` - Motion, GSAP, Rive, CSS scroll animations
- `ui-components-2025` - Magic UI, Aceternity, Motion Primitives, Origin UI
- `react-19-patterns` - Server Components, Actions, useActionState
- `css-2025` - Scroll-driven animations, anchor positioning, :has()

**Deployment & Infrastructure**
- `deploy-site`, `vercel-deploy`, `vercel-ai-deploy`
- `supabase-ops`, `supabase-master`

**Other**
- `agent-builder`, `ai-agent-builder`, `api-integrator`
- `fullstack-generator`, `ui-ux-modernizer`, `shadcn-ui`
- `vapi-voice-agent`, `hume-ai`
- `algorithmic-art`, `canvas-design`, `artifacts-builder`, `theme-factory`
- `webapp-testing`, `test-runner`

## Command Templates

Templates in `~/.claude/command-templates/` can be initialized in any project:

```bash
~/.claude/init-project-commands.sh --list           # List all
~/.claude/init-project-commands.sh                  # Init all in current project
~/.claude/init-project-commands.sh deep-debug tdd-cycle  # Init specific ones
```

Available: `deep-debug`, `smart-fix`, `tdd-cycle`, `feature-development`, `security-scan`, `deploy-checklist`, `db-migrate`, `api-scaffold`, `ai-assistant`, `deep-research`, `production-audit`, `stack-research`

**Frontend Commands (Simple & Powerful)**
- `/frontend` - Build a component with animations (auto-detects stack)
- `/responsive` - Analyze and fix responsiveness for all screens
- `/frontend-debug` - Debug visual bugs, layout issues, CSS conflicts

**Frontend Commands (Specific)**
- `/ui-build` - Build UI with 2025 best practices
- `/animate` - Add animations (Motion, GSAP, CSS, Rive)
- `/component-library` - Set up shadcn/ui, Magic UI, Aceternity
- `/react-19` - Implement with React 19 patterns
- `/css-modern` - Apply CSS 2025 features

## Specialized Agents

### project-debugger (`agents/project-debugger.md`)
Deep debugging for complex projects. Uses 6-phase methodology:
1. Information Gathering → 2. Hypothesis Formation → 3. Systematic Testing → 4. Root Cause Identification → 5. Fix Implementation → 6. Prevention

**Tools**: Read, Grep, Glob, Bash, Edit

## Installed Plugin: superpowers-dev

Located in `plugins/marketplaces/superpowers-dev/`, provides:
- **Commands**: `/brainstorm`, `/write-plan`, `/execute-plan`
- **Skills**: systematic-debugging, test-driven-development, root-cause-tracing, defense-in-depth, subagent-driven-development, code-review workflows, git worktrees

## Workflow Settings (Current)

```json
{
  "workflowMode": "explore-plan-code-commit",
  "testDrivenDevelopment": true,
  "exploreBeforeCoding": true,
  "createPlansFirst": true,
  "contextFiles": ["CLAUDE.md", "README.md", ".clauderc"]
}
```

This enforces: explore codebase → plan with TodoWrite → implement → commit

## State Directories

- `projects/` - Per-project state (path-encoded directories)
- `todos/` - Task tracking across sessions
- `file-history/` - File modification tracking
- `debug/` - Agent execution traces
- `plans/` - Saved development plans
- `session-env/` - Session environment state

## Credentials

- `.env.claude` - MCP server API keys (source before starting)
- `.credentials.json` - OAuth tokens (chmod 600)

